avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76705401?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordyfel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T15:18:12Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T15:18:12Z","body":"I do not understand where a potential slowdown would be so I'm not sure what load process should be measured.\r\n\r\nAs I understand it, this is GPU compression, so the textures never get decompressed, except for use by the GPU, which also has hardware acceleration for it so it happens very fast. All the textures are added to the decal atlas on scene load as before, with the only difference being that they are now GPU compressed, which shouldn't slow anything down since the copying happens in a shader on the GPU, right?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794199225/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794335367","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102857#issuecomment-2794335367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102857","id":2794335367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mjiyH","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T15:54:42Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T15:56:00Z","body":"> As I understand it, this is GPU compression, so the textures never get decompressed, except for use by the GPU, which also has hardware acceleration for it so it happens very fast. All the textures are added to the decal atlas on scene load as before, with the only difference being that they are now GPU compressed, which shouldn't slow anything down since the copying happens in a shader on the GPU, right?\r\n\r\nIf Godot copies a VRAM-compressed texture to an atlas, it is no longer VRAM-compressed in the atlas because textures can't be VRAM-compressed in real-time (in Godot at least). This means no VRAM is saved, but quality is decreased due to the use of VRAM compression on the source texture.\r\n\r\nI tend to agree with clayjohn we shouldn't make decal/projector textures use Detect 3D because of this. If we really want to, we'd have to add a special Detect 3D mode that enables mipmap generation and the roughness limiter but doesn't enable VRAM compression.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794335367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794389806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102857#issuecomment-2794389806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102857","id":2794389806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mjwEu","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T16:11:33Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T16:11:33Z","body":"> I do not understand where a potential slowdown would be so I'm not sure what load process should be measured.\r\n> \r\n> As I understand it, this is GPU compression, so the textures never get decompressed, except for use by the GPU, which also has hardware acceleration for it so it happens very fast. All the textures are added to the decal atlas on scene load as before, with the only difference being that they are now GPU compressed, which shouldn't slow anything down since the copying happens in a shader on the GPU, right?\r\n\r\nMy question is actually whether you see a load time _improvement_ from this change. It won't help at run time since these textures aren't used at run time. So the only thing this change would help is the time it takes to load the texture and blit it into the atlas. However, I think the difference will be so small that you may not even be able to measure it","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794389806/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794492008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102857#issuecomment-2794492008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102857","id":2794492008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mkJBo","user":{"login":"Jordyfel","id":76705401,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NzA1NDAx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76705401?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordyfel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T16:42:59Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T16:43:35Z","body":">If Godot copies a VRAM-compressed texture to an atlas, it is no longer VRAM-compressed in the atlas because textures can't be VRAM-compressed in real-time (in Godot at least)\r\n\r\nI had totally overlooked this part. It makes sense now that it wouldn't result in much of a performance gain.\r\n\r\nIt would make sense that the roughness filter still has an effect, since it changes the data of the texture itself, right? I'm not sure if it is important enough to warrant adding to the textures added to the atlas","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794492008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794923926","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102857#issuecomment-2794923926","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102857","id":2794923926,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mlyeW","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T19:18:02Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T19:18:02Z","body":"> It would make sense that the roughness filter still has an effect, since it changes the data of the texture itself, right? I'm not sure if it is important enough to warrant adding to the textures added to the atlas\r\n\r\nThat's a good point. I think so. And maybe the normal callback too? Can you check if the decal atlas includes the full mip chain and if it uses compressed normals?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794923926/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]